      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "\n{\n  \"presentation_title\": \"IR Spectroscopy\",\n  \"presentation_subtitle\": \"Principles, Interpretation and Applications\",\n  \"slide2_title\": \"Introduction to IR Spectroscopy\",\n  \"slide2_points\": \"• IR spectroscopy studies molecular vibrations.\\n• Molecules absorb specific infrared frequencies.\\n• Absorption patterns help identify functional groups.\",\n  \"slide3_title\": \"Fundamental Principles\",\n  \"slide3_points\": \"• Chemical bonds undergo stretching and bending vibrations.\\n• Absorption occurs at characteristic frequencies.\\n• Wavenumber is commonly measured in cm-1.\",\n  \"slide4_title\": \"Understanding IR Spectra\",\n  \"slide4_points\": \"• The functional group region ranges from approximately 4000 to 1500 cm-1.\\n• The fingerprint region ranges from approximately 1500 to 500 cm-1.\\n• Absorption bands help identify chemical bonds.\",\n  \"slide5_title\": \"Applications of IR Spectroscopy\",\n  \"slide5_points\": \"• Identifying functional groups in organic compounds.\\n• Checking the purity of chemical samples.\\n• Monitoring chemical reactions and materials.\",\n  \"slide6_title\": \"Conclusion\",\n  \"slide6_points\": \"• IR spectroscopy provides information about molecular vibrations.\\n• Characteristic absorption bands help identify functional groups.\\n• It is an important analytical technique in chemistry.\"\n}\n"
      },
